In https://github.com/flutter/packages/pull/13263, we updated `IconButton` to resolve its style variant via `IconButtonTheme.variantOf(context)`, which walks up enclosing `IconButtonTheme` widgets and returns the first non-null `variant`. This allows an inner `IconButtonTheme` with `variant: null` (such as the internal themes created by `AppBar`, `ListTile`, or `InputDecorator`) to override `style` without resetting an ancestor's `StyleVariant` (e.g., `StyleVariant.material3Expressive`).

However, this approach does not work across routes that capture themes using `InheritedTheme.capture` or `InheritedTheme.captureAll` (such as `showDialog`, `showModalBottomSheet`, and `PopupMenuButton`).

`InheritedTheme.capture` only records the closest `InheritedTheme` instance for each `runtimeType`. When a widget tree has an outer `IconButtonTheme` that sets `variant` and an inner `IconButtonTheme` with `variant: null`, capturing themes from inside the inner theme only captures the inner `IconButtonTheme`. In the new route, `IconButtonTheme.variantOf` cannot see the outer `IconButtonTheme` and falls back to `ThemeData.iconButtonTheme.variant` or `StyleVariant.material3`.

### Reproduction

The following test demonstrates the issue:

```dart
testWidgets('InheritedTheme.captureAll preserves the inherited variant', (
  WidgetTester tester,
) async {
  StyleVariant? capturedVariant;
  await tester.pumpWidget(
    MaterialApp(
      home: IconButtonTheme(
        data: const IconButtonThemeData(variant: StyleVariant.material3Expressive),
        child: IconButtonTheme(
          data: const IconButtonThemeData(
            style: ButtonStyle(foregroundColor: WidgetStatePropertyAll<Color>(Color(0xffff0000))),
          ),
          child: Builder(
            builder: (BuildContext context) {
              return ElevatedButton(
                onPressed: () {
                  Navigator.of(context).push(
                    MaterialPageRoute<void>(
                      builder: (BuildContext routeContext) {
                        return InheritedTheme.captureAll(
                          context,
                          Builder(
                            builder: (BuildContext innerContext) {
                              capturedVariant = IconButtonTheme.variantOf(innerContext);
                              return const SizedBox();
                            },
                          ),
                        );
                      },
                    ),
                  );
                },
                child: const Text('Push'),
              );
            },
          ),
        ),
      ),
    ),
  );

  await tester.tap(find.text('Push'));
  await tester.pumpAndSettle();

  // Fails: capturedVariant is StyleVariant.material3 instead of StyleVariant.material3Expressive.
  expect(capturedVariant, StyleVariant.material3Expressive);
