### Target platform

Linux desktop, x64. Measured on a physical laptop using an Xvfb X11 display (1366 × 768 × 24). Manjaro Linux, kernel `6.18.55-1-MANJARO`. This was not measured on another desktop compositor or on a second machine. The stable build uses its default Impeller OpenGLES backend and emits DRI3 warnings under Xvfb.

### Measurements

These are **post-GC** readings after actions 120 and 720 in the standalone sample, with no native profiler or object-counter library loaded:

| Flutter SDK | RssAnon at action 120 | RssAnon at action 720 | Increase | Dart heap at both checkpoints | Live Dart SemanticsNode instances at both checkpoints |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| 3.32.7 stable | 119.22 MiB | 135.32 MiB | 16.11 MiB | 6,027,872 bytes | 40 |
| 3.47.9 stable | 227.82 MiB | 240.18 MiB | 12.36 MiB | 6,459,840 bytes | 40 |

No Dart class gained instances between those checkpoints in either run. `RssAnon` is resident anonymous memory, not total private memory or total live allocations. MiB is binary; heaptrack's MB below is decimal. These runs establish reproduction, not a comparison of renderer efficiency or a universal per-page allocation rate. The two normal runs overlapped in time; no timing comparison is claimed.

### Native object lifetime on 3.47.9

In a separate diagnostic run, an `LD_PRELOAD` probe intercepted `g_object_new`, checked the registered GType name for `FlAccessibleNode`, and attached a weak notification to count finalization:

| Checkpoint | FlAccessibleNode objects constructed | Finalized |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| Initial frame, after GC | 40 | 0 |
| 120 actions, after GC | 3,880 | 0 |
| After idle and another GC | 3,880 | 0 |

That is **3,840 additional native accessibility nodes, 32 per action**, with no finalization during this interval. The probe adds weak-reference bookkeeping, so its process-memory figures are not used in the table above. A control process that constructed and released a test GObject with the matching type name reported one creation and one finalization; the weak notification does not keep the object alive.

<details><summary>Optional node_counter.c diagnostic</summary>

Build with `cc -shared -fPIC node_counter.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs gobject-2.0) -ldl -o node_counter.so`. Run the harness with `--preload /absolute/path/to/node_counter.so --steps 120 --idle 1`. This probe is not needed to reproduce the growth.

```c
// Optional native diagnostic. Count FlAccessibleNode construction/finalization even
// when the official engine library has no local function symbols.
// Build: cc -shared -fPIC node_counter.c $(pkg-config --cflags --libs gobject-2.0) -ldl -o node_counter.so
#define _GNU_SOURCE
#include <dlfcn.h>
#include <glib-object.h>
#include <stdarg.h>
#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

static unsigned long created;
static unsigned long freed;

static void finalized(gpointer data, GObject* object) {
  (void)data;
  (void)object;
  freed++;
  fprintf(stderr, "[node-counter] created=%lu freed=%lu\n", created, freed);
}

gpointer g_object_new(GType type, const gchar* first_property_name, ...) {
  static GObject* (*original_valist)(GType, const gchar*, va_list);
  if (original_valist == NULL) original_valist = dlsym(RTLD_NEXT, "g_object_new_valist");
  va_list args;
  va_start(args, first_property_name);
  GObject* object = original_valist(type, first_property_name, args);
  va_end(args);
  const char* name = g_type_name(type);
  if (object != NULL && name != NULL && strcmp(name, "FlAccessibleNode") == 0) {
    created++;
    // Weak notification observes finalization without retaining the object.
    // The extra weak-reference bookkeeping belongs only to this diagnostic.
    g_object_weak_ref(object, finalized, NULL);
    fprintf(stderr, "[node-counter] created=%lu freed=%lu\n", created, freed);
  }
  return object;
}
```

