### Steps to reproduce

The engine is contacted only when the last handle is disposed, and then only to request `DartPerformanceMode.balanced`:

```dart
// packages/flutter/lib/src/scheduler/binding.dart
PerformanceModeRequestHandle? requestPerformanceMode(DartPerformanceMode mode) {
  // conflicting requests are not allowed.
  if (_performanceMode != null && _performanceMode != mode) {
    return null;
  }

  if (_performanceMode == mode) {
    assert(_numPerformanceModeRequests > 0);
    _numPerformanceModeRequests++;
  } else if (_performanceMode == null) {
    assert(_numPerformanceModeRequests == 0);
    _performanceMode = mode;
    _numPerformanceModeRequests = 1;
    // <-- no PlatformDispatcher.instance.requestDartPerformanceMode(mode) here
  }

  return PerformanceModeRequestHandle._(_disposePerformanceModeRequest);
}

void _disposePerformanceModeRequest() {
  _numPerformanceModeRequests--;
  if (_numPerformanceModeRequests == 0) {
    _performanceMode = null;
    PlatformDispatcher.instance.requestDartPerformanceMode(DartPerformanceMode.balanced);
  }
}
```

There is minimal reproduction that exhibits the difference between calling this API with directly invoking `ui.PlatformDispatcher.instance.requestDartPerformanceMode` 

**Repro Steps**:

1. Run the code sample on an Android device in profile mode with systrace output, once per mode:
   ```
   flutter run --profile --trace-systrace --dart-define=MODE=none
   flutter run --profile --trace-systrace --dart-define=MODE=handle
   flutter run --profile --trace-systrace --dart-define=MODE=direct
   ```
2. Capture a Perfetto trace for a fixed window (for example 30 s) with the `gfx`, `view` and `dalvik` atrace categories and `atrace_apps` set to the app's package.
3. Count the engine idle notifications and GCs on the UI thread:
   ```sql
   select s.name, count(*) as n, round(sum(s.dur) / 1e6, 2) as total_ms
   from slice s
   join thread_track tt on s.track_id = tt.id
   join thread t using (utid)
   join process p using (upid)
   where p.name = '<your.package.name>'
     and s.name in ('Dart_NotifyIdle', 'CollectNewGeneration', 'CollectOldGeneration')
   group by 1 order by 1;
   ```

### Expected results

Handle mode and direct mode should behave the same, having a much smaller GC counts compared to none.

### Actual results

| Variant | `Dart_NotifyIdle` | `CollectNewGeneration` | `CollectOldGeneration` (n / total ms) |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| No request (`none`) | 1007 | 352 | 268 / 457.9 |
| `requestPerformanceMode(latency)` only (`handle`) | 1005 | 362 | 275 / 389.6 |
| Handle + `requestDartPerformanceMode(latency)` (`direct`) | 10 | 106 | 8 / 10.4 |

calling `requestDartPerformanceMode(latency)` behaves not differently compared to no request at all.

