### Use case

The Linux embedder enables semantics when the engine starts. `fl_engine_start()` calls `UpdateSemanticsEnabled(self->engine, TRUE)` with no condition (added in flutter/engine#19634, not changed since). So the framework builds and updates the semantics tree on every frame, also when no screen reader or other assistive technology is running.

The other desktop embedders do not do this. The Windows embedder enables semantics when a UIA or MSAA client queries the window (`WM_GETOBJECT`, flutter/engine#29269). The macOS embedder starts with semantics off.

### Cost

A benchmark at the rendering layer only (code below): N `RenderParagraph`s change their text, then the pipeline flushes layout, compositing bits, paint and semantics. It counts the flushes that fit in a fixed 300 ms window. Whether semantics are flushed is decided only by the engine. Profile build, i7-8850H, performance governor, 3 interleaved rounds of 10 windows, median (range):

| Paragraphs | master (semantics on) | Proposal, no assistive technology (off) | Proposal, client connected (on) |
|---|---|---|---|
| 50 | 165 (164–166) | 206 (204–210), +25% | 168 (164–168) |
| 200 | 41 (39–41) | 52 (50–53), +27% | 41 (39–41) |
| 1000 | 8 (8–8) | 10 (9–10), +25% | 8 (8–8) |

So when text changes, semantics take about a fifth of the pipeline time at every size, and nobody uses the result.

<details>
<summary>Benchmark</summary>

Run it as a Linux app (`flutter build linux --profile`). Set `N` for the number of paragraphs.

```dart
// Counts how many pipeline flushes fit in fixed 300 ms windows while every
// paragraph changes text. Rendering layer only, no widgets. Whether semantics
// are flushed is decided by the engine (PlatformDispatcher.semanticsEnabled).
import 'dart:async';
import 'dart:convert';
import 'dart:io';

import 'package:flutter/rendering.dart';

const _window = Duration(milliseconds: 300);

void main() async {
  final binding = RenderingFlutterBinding.ensureInitialized();
  final n = int.parse(Platform.environment['N'] ?? '200');
  final windows = int.parse(Platform.environment['WINDOWS'] ?? '10');

  // Give the AT-SPI monitor time to see a client that is already there.
  await Future<void>.delayed(const Duration(seconds: 2));

  const style = TextStyle(fontSize: 14, color: Color(0xff000000));
  final paragraphs = [
    for (var i = 0; i < n; i++)
      RenderParagraph(
        TextSpan(text: 'row $i 0.00', style: style),
        textDirection: TextDirection.ltr,
      ),
  ];
  // Without runApp the render view has to be wired up by hand, see
  // RendererBinding.renderView.
  final view = binding.renderView;
  final viewOwner = binding.pipelineOwner;
  binding.rootPipelineOwner.adoptChild(viewOwner);
  viewOwner.rootNode = view;
  binding.addRenderView(view);
  view.child = RenderFlex(direction: Axis.vertical, children: paragraphs);
  view.prepareInitialFrame();
  final owner = binding.rootPipelineOwner;

  var tick = 0;
  void step() {
    tick++;
    for (var i = 0; i < n; i++) {
      paragraphs[i].text = TextSpan(
        text: 'row $i ${(tick * 7 + i) % 1000}.${tick % 100}',
        style: style,
      );
    }
    owner
      ..flushLayout()
      ..flushCompositingBits()
      ..flushPaint()
      ..flushSemantics();
  }

  // Warm up.
  for (var i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
    step();
  }

  final counts = <int>[];
  for (var w = 0; w < windows; w++) {
    final sw = Stopwatch()..start();
    var count = 0;
    while (sw.elapsed < _window) {
      step();
      count++;
    }
    counts.add(count);
    // Let the event loop run between windows.
    await Future<void>.delayed(Duration.zero);
  }
  final sorted = [...counts]..sort();
  stdout.writeln(
    'SEM300 ${jsonEncode({
      'semanticsEnabled': binding.semanticsEnabled,
      'laidOut': paragraphs.first.hasSize,
      'semanticsNodes': binding.pipelineOwner.semanticsOwner?.rootSemanticsNode == null ? 0 : 1,
      'n': n,
      'median_flushes_per_300ms': sorted[sorted.length ~/ 2],
      'all': counts,
    })}',
  );
  exit(0);
}
