### Steps to reproduce

1. Lay out an RTL paragraph (`TextDirection.rtl`) with two identical Hebrew lines separated by a hard line break: `'שלום עולם טוב\nשלום עולם טוב'`, width 400, a real font (Arial).
2. Compare `getBoxesForSelection` / `getPositionForOffset` on line 1 (terminated by `\n`) with line 2 (the last line, same text).
3. Compare with where the glyphs are actually painted.

The same happens with U+2028 and U+2029, with any `TextAlign` (start, right, left, center, justify), with `TextPainter`, `Text`/`SelectionArea` and `SelectableText`. A space before the break (`' \n'`) or `\r\n` does not trigger it. Found in an RTL Hebrew reader app (selection highlight of the last line of every paragraph stuck out to the right, and drag selection picked a neighbouring character).

### Expected results

Line 1 measures like line 2: the boxes and hit-testing match the painted glyphs, and the line does not extend past the paragraph width.

### Actual results

In the line that ends with the hard break, every box and every `getPositionForOffset` result is shifted right by the advance of the line-break glyph (15 px with Arial at 20 px, i.e. its .notdef advance 0.75em; 9 px with another Hebrew font at 24 px). The glyphs themselves paint correctly. The break's own box is zero-width at the correct left edge, so the selection highlight sticks out past the right edge of the paragraph and leaves a gap on the left.

Output of the test below (Arial, font size 20, width 400):

```
U+000a
  line 1 (ends with U+000a) boxes : [299.52, 415.00]
  line 2 (last line)       boxes : [284.52, 400.00]
  hard break box                 : [284.52, 284.52]
  first char box  line1 / line2  : [401.11328125, 415.0] / [386.11328125, 400.0]
  painted ink x   line1 / line2  : [285, 399) / [285, 399)
  getPositionForOffset at painted center of first char, line 1: 2 (expected 0)
```

U+2028 and U+2029 print identical numbers. Other Windows fonts give the same picture: Tahoma +20 px, Times New Roman +15.6, Segoe UI +12.9, David +10. The `flutter_test` default font does not reproduce it (it gives the break no advance).

