### Steps to reproduce

In [`pipeline.h`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/b718471b2c2c/engine/src/flutter/shell/common/pipeline.h#L183-L253), `flutter::Pipeline` guards `queue_` with both `queue_mutex_` and an `available_` semaphore in opposite orders:

1. `ProducerCommit` (L224-L235) locks `queue_mutex_`, sets `is_first_item = queue_.empty()`, pushes to `queue_`, **unlocks `queue_mutex_`**, and then calls `available_.Signal()`.
2. [`Animator::EndFrame`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/b718471b2c2c/engine/src/flutter/shell/common/animator.cc#L162-L174) calls `OnAnimatorDraw` **only** when `result.is_first_item` is `true` (since `da7bae6`).
3. `Consume` (L183-L213) checks `available_.TryWait()` **before** locking `queue_mutex_`, pops the front item, and returns `MoreAvailable` if `queue_.size() > 0`. [`Rasterizer::Draw`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/b718471b2c2c/engine/src/flutter/shell/common/rasterizer.cc#L280-L321) reposts `Draw` only on `MoreAvailable`.

With pipeline depth `2` (Android, iOS Metal, Fuchsia, and desktop when platform != raster runner), this causes a permanent lost wakeup:

1. **Frame A** commits (`is_first_item = true`), calls `available_.Signal()` (`0 -> 1`), and posts `Draw_1`.
2. **Frame B** locks `queue_mutex_` on UI, sees `is_first_item = false`, pushes `B`, **unlocks `queue_mutex_`**, and is preempted before `available_.Signal()`. (On Android, [`android_shell_holder.cc`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/b718471b2c2c/engine/src/flutter/shell/platform/android/android_shell_holder.cc#L48-L68) sets `.raster` to `nice -5` above `.ui` at `nice -1`, so `FUTEX_WAKE` on unlock favors preempting `.ui`.)
3. `Draw_1` runs `Consume()`: `available_.TryWait()` (`1 -> 0`), pops `A`, sees `queue_.size() == 1` (`B`), returns `MoreAvailable`, and posts `Draw_2`.
4. `Draw_2` runs `Consume()`: `available_.TryWait()` is `false` (`0`), returns `NoneAvailable`, and exits without reposting.
5. UI resumes, calls `available_.Signal()` (`0 -> 1`), returns `is_first_item = false`, and skips `OnAnimatorDraw`. **Frame B is stranded.**
6. **Frame C** takes the second slot (`empty_: 1 -> 0`), sees `B` queued (`is_first_item = false`), pushes `C`, signals `available_` (`1 -> 2`), and skips `OnAnimatorDraw`.

Both slots stay full (`empty_ == 0, available_ == 2, queue_.size() == 2`) with `0` raster tasks; `OnPlatformViewDestroyed`/`Created` does not reset `layer_tree_pipeline_`.

### Expected results

`ProducerCommit` and `Consume` agree atomically on queue emptiness under `queue_mutex_` (`available_.Wait()` is never called, so `available_` is redundant).

### Actual results

Every subsequent VSync hits `PipelineFull` forever while Dart timers continue running and the raster thread sleeps idle (`ALooper_pollOnce` on Android, `zx_port_wait` on Fuchsia).

### Code sample

```cpp
// g++ -std=c++17 -O2 -pthread repro.cc -o repro && ./repro
#include <errno.h>
#include <semaphore.h>
#include <cstdio>
#include <deque>
#include <functional>
#include <mutex>

struct Sem {
  sem_t s{};
  explicit Sem(uint32_t c) { ::sem_init(&s, 0, c); }
  ~Sem() { ::sem_destroy(&s); }
  bool TryWait() {
    int r;
    do { r = ::sem_trywait(&s); } while (r == -1 && errno == EINTR);
    return r == 0;
  }
  void Signal() { ::sem_post(&s); }
  int Val() { int v = -1; ::sem_getvalue(&s, &v); return v; }
};

struct UnpatchedPipeline {
  Sem empty{2}, avail{0};
  std::mutex mu;
  std::deque<int> q;
  std::function<void()> hook;
  bool Produce() { return empty.TryWait(); }
  bool Commit(int f) {
    bool first = false;
    { std::scoped_lock lk(mu); first = q.empty(); q.push_back(f); }
    if (hook) hook();
    avail.Signal();
    return first;
  }
  int Consume() {  // 0=NoneAvailable, 1=Done, 2=MoreAvailable
    if (!avail.TryWait()) return 0;
    size_t rem = 0;
    { std::scoped_lock lk(mu); q.pop_front(); rem = q.size(); }
    empty.Signal();
    return rem > 0 ? 2 : 1;
  }
};

int main() {
  std::deque<std::function<void()>> rq;
  int n = 0;
  UnpatchedPipeline p;
  std::function<void()> draw = [&] { if (p.Consume() == 2) rq.push_back(draw); };
  p.hook = [&] {
    if (++n == 2) while (!rq.empty()) { auto f = rq.front(); rq.pop_front(); f(); }
  };
  auto frame = [&](int f) {
    if (!p.Produce()) return false;
    if (p.Commit(f)) rq.push_back(draw);
    return true;
  };
  frame(1); frame(2); frame(3);
  std::printf("empty=%d avail=%d queue=%zu raster_tasks=%zu frame4=%d\n",
              p.empty.Val(), p.avail.Val(), p.q.size(), rq.size(), frame(4));
}
