### Steps to reproduce

1. Run the sample below on a Linux RK3576 with the proprietary Mali-G52 g24p0 driver and the GTK/Wayland embedder. We tested Flutter main `c08f4b8252ea` (`3.51.0-1.0.pre-88`), Linux 6.1.141 and Weston 14.0.2 at 1920 × 1080.
2. Enable Impeller. In the Linux runner, call `fl_dart_project_set_enable_impeller(project, TRUE)` before creating the view. Our run logged `Using the Impeller rendering backend (OpenGLESSDF)`.
3. Let the white START screen transition to the two animated pages. The sample prints the page number as it switches.

### Expected results

Each page repaints the window. PAGE 1 shows a rounded cyan rectangle; PAGE 2 shows a clipped gradient. The START screen disappears.

### Actual results

Large regions of the START screen remain visible across both page changes, including lettering and the red and green bars. Only parts of the new shapes and text appear. The same release AOT and assets paint both pages correctly with Skia.

On this board we also tried compiling just the built-in ESSL 300 fragment uniform blocks as plain uniforms. This eliminated the stale content with Impeller in both the sample and a calendar app. Vertex shaders, runtime shaders and SSBO shaders were unchanged. We haven't established why the UBO path produces different pixels.

`GL_RENDERER=Mali-G52`, `GL_VERSION=OpenGL ES 3.2 v1.g24p0-00eac0.fe7fa84c52ed3b756cd64cb3246aafd9`, `GL_MAX_FRAGMENT_UNIFORM_VECTORS=4096`.

