### Steps to reproduce

An `OverlayPortal` whose overlay is inside another `OverlayPortal`'s child (for example a `Tooltip` around `Overlay.wrap(child: Slider(...))`) makes the framework list the inner overlay child under two semantics parents in `childrenInTraversalOrder`: its own traversal parent and its hit-test parent. On Windows the update is rejected:

```
[ERROR:flutter/shell/platform/common/accessibility_bridge.cc(114)] Failed to update ui::AXTree, error: Node 310 is already pending for creation, cannot be a new child
```

The outer portal does not have to be showing anything. It happens on stable 3.47.7 and on master (6b2bb92cec).

1. Run the test below with `flutter test`. It records every semantics update and checks that each node has a single parent.

### Expected results

Each node is listed by one parent. The inner overlay child is listed only under the inner portal's traversal parent.

### Actual results

```
[3 listed under 2 and 1]
```

Node 1 is the outer portal's traversal parent and the hit-test parent of the inner overlay child (node 3). `SemanticsNode._updateChildrenInTraversalOrder` only grafts a traversal child away when its hit-test parent is not a traversal parent at all (`!_isTraversalParent`), so node 1 keeps it, and node 2 (its real traversal parent) adds it too. `_childrenInHitTestOrder` and `_shouldSkipInHitTest` make the same check, so when the inner portal's anchor is missing (for example under `Opacity(opacity: 0)`), the inner overlay child is sent as an orphan in traversal order.

