### Steps to reproduce

1. Create a macOS app (`flutter create --platforms=macos`), replace `lib/main.dart` with the code below, and add `FLTEnableImpeller = true` to `macos/Runner/Info.plist`.
2. `flutter build macos --profile`, then run the binary with `MODE=gradient`.
3. Watch `footprint -p <pid>` (`phys_footprint`) while the blur sigma animates.

The app draws one oval that is much larger than the visible area (3600×2500 logical px on a 402×874 canvas scaled ×3, clipped to the canvas) with a linear gradient shader and an animated `MaskFilter.blur`.

### Expected results

Memory stays bounded by the clipped, visible area, as it does on 3.47.9 and as it does on 3.50.0 with a solid color.

### Actual results

On 3.50.0 the process footprint follows the blur animation up to about 4 GB. On an iPhone 14 Pro (iOS 27.0.1) the same drawing, coming from a Lottie animation in our app, gets the app killed by jetsam at 3.2–3.6 GB (`per-process-limit`) a few seconds after launch, with the UI frozen.

Peak `phys_footprint`, GitHub-hosted `macos-15` runner (macOS 15.8.2, arm64), profile build, Impeller (Metal):

| MODE | 3.47.9 | 3.50.0 |
|---|---|---|
| `small` (gradient, shape inside the viewport) | 106 MB | 114 MB |
| `solid` (large shape, solid color) | 54 MB | 51 MB |
| `gradient` (large shape, linear gradient) | 99 MB | **4146 MB** |

Samples every ~0.2 s for `gradient` on 3.50.0 (MB): `1291 1740 2231 725 726 … 904 2595 3411 4146 734 732 … 3885 819 …`

Limiting the sigma does not help (we still saw 3.5 GB with a radius of 20 in the original animation), so the cost seems to scale with the path bounds rather than with the clipped area or the blur radius.

Possibly related: #194832, #191457.

### Code sample

```dart
// Minimal reproduction: MaskFilter.blur on a path much larger than the
// viewport. MODE = gradient | solid | small (env var), default gradient.
import 'dart:io';
import 'dart:ui' as ui;

import 'package:flutter/widgets.dart';

final mode = Platform.environment['MODE'] ?? 'gradient';

void main() => runApp(const _App());

class _App extends StatefulWidget {
  const _App();
  @override
  State<_App> createState() => _AppState();
}

class _AppState extends State<_App> with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {
  late final AnimationController _c = AnimationController(
    vsync: this,
    duration: const Duration(seconds: 2),
  )..repeat(reverse: true);
  var _frames = 0;

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    _c.addListener(() {
      if (++_frames % 30 == 0) {
        stdout.writeln('APP [$mode] frame=$_frames sigma=${_sigma.round()}');
      }
      if (_frames > 600) exit(0);
    });
  }

  double get _sigma => 1 + 76 * _c.value;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => CustomPaint(
    painter: _Painter(mode, _c, () => _sigma),
    size: Size.infinite,
  );
}

class _Painter extends CustomPainter {
  _Painter(this.mode, Listenable repaint, this.sigma) : super(repaint: repaint);
  final String mode;
  final double Function() sigma;

  @override
  void paint(Canvas canvas, Size size) {
    // A 402x874 logical canvas at device pixel ratio 3 (iPhone 14 Pro).
    canvas.clipRect(const Rect.fromLTWH(0, 0, 1179, 2556));
    canvas.scale(3);
    // The shape is far larger than the visible area; only a part is on screen.
    final rect = mode == 'small'
        ? const Rect.fromLTWH(50, 200, 300, 400)
        : const Rect.fromLTWH(-1600, -800, 3600, 2500);
    final paint = Paint()
      ..maskFilter = MaskFilter.blur(BlurStyle.normal, sigma());
    if (mode == 'solid') {
      paint.color = const Color(0xFFE8642D);
    } else {
      paint.shader = ui.Gradient.linear(
        rect.centerLeft,
        rect.centerRight,
        const [Color(0xFFE8642D), Color(0xFFB8300C)],
      );
    }
    canvas.drawPath(Path()..addOval(rect), paint);
  }

  @override
  bool shouldRepaint(_Painter old) => true;
}
```

