### Steps to reproduce

1. `flutter create bug`
2. Replace `bug/test/widget_test.dart` with the code sample below.
3. `cd bug` and `flutter test`

The `ClipRect` test passes; the other tests fail.

### Expected results

The semantics rect of a child is clipped by the clip its parent applies in `paint`, as it is under `ClipRect`:

https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/object.dart#L3755-L3768

### Actual results

The following render objects clip their children in `paint` but don't override `describeApproximatePaintClip`, so the semantics rect of a clipped child is not clipped. Results on Flutter 3.50.0, where only the top half of a 100x100 child is inside the clip:

| Widget | Render object | Expected semantics rect | Actual semantics rect | Result |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `ClipRect` (reference) | `RenderClipRect` | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 50)` | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 50)` | Correct |
| `Wrap` | [`RenderWrap`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/wrap.dart#L843-L851) | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 50)` | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 100)` | Wrong.<br>The second run overflows the `Wrap` and is clipped, but its semantics rect is not. |
| `FittedBox` | [`RenderFittedBox`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/proxy_box.dart#L3008-L3016) | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 50)` | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 100)` | Wrong.<br>The child is taller than the `FittedBox` and is clipped, but its semantics rect is not. |
| `Flow` | [`RenderFlow`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/flow.dart#L408-L415) | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 50)` | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 100)` | Wrong.<br>The delegate paints the child 50 down, where it is clipped, but its semantics rect is not. |
| `Text.rich` | [`RenderParagraph`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/paragraph.dart#L1072-L1091) | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 50)` | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 100)` | Wrong.<br>The second line overflows the text and is clipped, but its semantics rect is not. |
| `TwoDimensionalViewport` | [`RenderTwoDimensionalViewport`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/packages/flutter/lib/src/widgets/two_dimensional_viewport.dart#L1640-L1657) | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 50)` | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 100)` | Wrong.<br>The second child overflows the viewport and is clipped, but its semantics rect is not. |
| `AnimatedSize` | [`RenderAnimatedSize`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/animated_size.dart#L386-L395) | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 50)` | `Rect.fromLTRB(0, 0, 100, 100)` | Wrong.<br>The `AnimatedSize` is 50 high while growing and clips the child, but its semantics rect is not clipped. |

Related: #103748 and #103931 fixed the opposite case, render objects that described a clip they did not apply.


### Code sample

<details open><summary>Code sample</summary>

```dart
import 'package:flutter/rendering.dart';
import 'package:flutter/widgets.dart';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';

void main() {
  final cases = <String, Widget>{
    'ClipRect (reference)': const ClipRect(
      child: OverflowBox(
        alignment: .topLeft,
        maxHeight: double.infinity,
        child: Column(children: [SizedBox(height: 50), _Target()]),
      ),
    ),
    'Wrap': const Wrap(
      clipBehavior: .hardEdge,
      children: [SizedBox(width: 100, height: 50), _Target()],
    ),
    'FittedBox': const FittedBox(
      fit: .none,
      alignment: .topLeft,
      clipBehavior: .hardEdge,
      child: Column(children: [SizedBox(height: 50), _Target()]),
    ),
    'Flow': Flow(
      delegate: _OffsetFlow(),
      clipBehavior: .hardEdge,
      children: const [_Target()],
    ),
    'Text.rich': const Text.rich(
      TextSpan(
        children: [
          WidgetSpan(child: SizedBox(width: 100, height: 50)),
          WidgetSpan(child: _Target()),
        ],
      ),
      overflow: .clip,
    ),
    'TwoDimensionalViewport': _Grid(
      children: const [SizedBox(width: 100, height: 50), _Target()],
    ),
    'AnimatedSize': const _Growing(),
  };

  for (final MapEntry(:key, :value) in cases.entries) {
    testWidgets('$key clips the semantics rect of a half clipped child', (
      tester,
    ) async {
      final handle = tester.ensureSemantics();
      await tester.pumpWidget(
        Directionality(
          textDirection: .ltr,
          child: Align(
            alignment: .topLeft,
            child: SizedBox(width: 100, height: 100, child: value),
          ),
        ),
      );
      await tester.pump();
      await tester.pump(const Duration(milliseconds: 500));
      expect(
        tester.getSemantics(find.bySemanticsLabel('target')).rect.height,
        50,
        reason: 'Only the top half of the target is inside the clip.',
      );
      handle.dispose();
    });
  }
}

class _Target extends StatelessWidget {
  const _Target();

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Semantics(
      label: 'target',
      container: true,
      child: const SizedBox(width: 100, height: 100),
    );
  }
}

class _OffsetFlow extends FlowDelegate {
  @override
  void paintChildren(FlowPaintingContext context) {
    context.paintChild(0, transform: .translationValues(0, 50, 0));
  }

  @override
  bool shouldRepaint(_OffsetFlow oldDelegate) => false;
}

// Minimal implementation of RenderTwoDimensionalViewport for this test,
// laying out the children in a column.
class _Grid extends TwoDimensionalScrollView {
  _Grid({required List<Widget> children})
    : super(delegate: TwoDimensionalChildListDelegate(children: [children]));

  @override
  Widget buildViewport(
    BuildContext context,
    ViewportOffset verticalOffset,
    ViewportOffset horizontalOffset,
  ) {
    return _GridViewport(
      verticalOffset: verticalOffset,
      verticalAxisDirection: verticalDetails.direction,
      horizontalOffset: horizontalOffset,
      horizontalAxisDirection: horizontalDetails.direction,
      mainAxis: mainAxis,
      delegate: delegate,
    );
  }
}

class _GridViewport extends TwoDimensionalViewport {
  const _GridViewport({
    required super.verticalOffset,
    required super.verticalAxisDirection,
    required super.horizontalOffset,
    required super.horizontalAxisDirection,
    required super.mainAxis,
    required super.delegate,
  });

  @override
  RenderTwoDimensionalViewport createRenderObject(BuildContext context) {
    return _RenderGrid(
      verticalOffset: verticalOffset,
      verticalAxisDirection: verticalAxisDirection,
      horizontalOffset: horizontalOffset,
      horizontalAxisDirection: horizontalAxisDirection,
      mainAxis: mainAxis,
      delegate: delegate,
      childManager: context as TwoDimensionalChildManager,
    );
  }
}

class _RenderGrid extends RenderTwoDimensionalViewport {
  _RenderGrid({
    required super.verticalOffset,
    required super.verticalAxisDirection,
    required super.horizontalOffset,
    required super.horizontalAxisDirection,
    required super.mainAxis,
    required super.delegate,
    required super.childManager,
  });

  @override
  void layoutChildSequence() {
    var top = 0.0;
    for (var x = 0; ; x++) {
      final child = buildOrObtainChildFor(ChildVicinity(xIndex: x, yIndex: 0));
      if (child == null) {
        break;
      }
      child.layout(const BoxConstraints(), parentUsesSize: true);
      parentDataOf(child).layoutOffset = Offset(0, top);
      top += child.size.height;
    }
    verticalOffset.applyContentDimensions(0, 0);
    horizontalOffset.applyContentDimensions(0, 0);
  }
}

// Grows an AnimatedSize from 0 to 100 high, so that it is 50 high after 500ms.
class _Growing extends StatefulWidget {
  const _Growing();

  @override
  State<_Growing> createState() => _GrowingState();
}

class _GrowingState extends State<_Growing> {
  var _grown = false;

  @override
  void initState() {
    super.initState();
    WidgetsBinding.instance.addPostFrameCallback(
      (_) => setState(() => _grown = true),
    );
  }

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Align(
      alignment: .topLeft,
      child: AnimatedSize(
        duration: const Duration(seconds: 1),
        alignment: .topLeft,
        child: _grown ? const _Target() : const SizedBox(width: 100),
      ),
    );
  }
}
