### Steps to reproduce

1. Run the code sample below.
2. The screen has a 16 px white band along its top edge, with a dark gradient below. Three equal bars along the top edge each apply a `BackdropFilter`:
   - **left:** `ImageFilter.blur(sigma 20)`, no tile mode;
   - **middle:** `ImageFilter.compose(outer: ColorFilter.matrix(identity), inner: ImageFilter.blur(sigma 20))`, no tile mode;
   - **right:** the same compose, but with `tileMode: TileMode.mirror` on the inner blur.
3. Compare the top edge of the three bars.

### Expected results

All three bars look the same. The color matrix is the identity. The [blur tile mode breaking change](https://docs.flutter.dev/release/breaking-changes/image-filter-blur-tilemode) says an unspecified tile mode means mirror for backdrop filters.

### Actual results

The middle bar is brighter along the top edge. Its blur smears the white edge row inward, as clamp does. The left and right bars match each other (mirror).

Measured on a screenshot (1440×3168, 3.5 px per dp). This is the mean luma (0-255) of icon-free columns of each bar, by distance from the top edge:

| From top | blur | compose | compose + mirror |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0 px (0 dp) | 181.0 | **217.8** | 181.0 |
| 10 px (2.9 dp) | 180.0 | **209.8** | 181.0 |
| 20 px (5.7 dp) | 176.0 | **190.9** | 174.0 |
| 40 px (11.4 dp) | 162.0 | **169.9** | 162.0 |
| 60 px (17.1 dp) and below | equal within ±5 | | |

The difference is up to +37 levels at the edge row and fades out within about 17 dp at sigma 20.

The middle and right bars also show 8 px bands where the left bar is smooth. That is a separate defect (nearest-neighbour sampling in the color matrix filter), filed as #196725.

In an app this shows as a one-frame brightness step. A common way to fade a backdrop blur is a composed alpha color matrix, and switching to the plain blur once the fade ends (to keep the filters equal for `BackdropGroup` sharing) changes the edge mode.

**Cause (engine source).**
- `ImageFilter.blur` with no tile mode is marked dynamic and is resolved where it is used. `SceneBuilder::pushBackdropFilter` resolves it with `kMirror`:
  - 3.47.9: [`lib/ui/painting/image_filter.cc#L72-L99`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/c197ca5199e9ee5661e865596c9c07294dfab51c/engine/src/flutter/lib/ui/painting/image_filter.cc#L72-L99)
  - 3.47.9: [`lib/ui/compositing/scene_builder.cc#L195`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/c197ca5199e9ee5661e865596c9c07294dfab51c/engine/src/flutter/lib/ui/compositing/scene_builder.cc#L195)
- `ImageFilter::initComposeFilter` resolves both children right away with `kClamp`, and the compose itself is not dynamic. So a compose used as a backdrop never gets mirror:
  - 3.47.9: [`lib/ui/painting/image_filter.cc#L127-L131`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/c197ca5199e9ee5661e865596c9c07294dfab51c/engine/src/flutter/lib/ui/painting/image_filter.cc#L127-L131)
- 3.50.0 is identical: [`image_filter.cc#L127-L131`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/engine/src/flutter/lib/ui/painting/image_filter.cc#L127-L131) and [`scene_builder.cc#L195`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/engine/src/flutter/lib/ui/compositing/scene_builder.cc#L195). `master` on 2026-11-16: the same.

**Possible fix.** Make a compose dynamic when either child is. Keep references to the child `ImageFilter`s and resolve them in `ImageFilter::filter(mode)` with the mode of the place the filter is used (mirror for backdrops), the way a lone blur is resolved.

**Docs.** The breaking-change page recommends removing explicit blur tile modes ("recommend removing any specified blur tile modes"). For a blur inside `ImageFilter.compose` used as a backdrop, that advice gives clamp, not mirror. Until this is fixed, the page should say that composed backdrop blurs need `tileMode: TileMode.mirror` set explicitly.

