### Steps to reproduce

Run the code sample below (its middle and right bars), or any `BackdropFilter` with `ImageFilter.compose(outer: ColorFilter.matrix(...), inner: ImageFilter.blur(sigma 20))` over a smooth vertical gradient. Compare it with the same `ImageFilter.blur` alone.

### Expected results

The composed blur is as smooth as the plain blur. The color matrix is per-pixel and, in this repro, the identity.

### Actual results

The composed blur shows hard bands, 8 px tall on this device. That matches Impeller's 1/8 downsample for sigma 20 at 3.5 px per dp. The plain blur is smooth.

Mean luma of one icon-free 60 px column, rows 100-179 below the top edge, from a 1440×3168 screenshot:

```
blur      88 87 86 85 84 83 82 81 80 79 77 76 75 74 73 72 71 70 70 69 ...  (smooth)
compose   84 84 84 84 84 84 84 84 76 76 76 76 76 76 76 76 68 68 68 68 ...  (steps of 8 rows)
```

The explicit-mirror compose shows exactly the same steps, so this is not the tile-mode issue.

**Cause (engine source).**
- `ColorMatrixFilterContents` samples its input snapshot with a default sampler: `GetSamplerLibrary()->GetSampler({})`. The default is `MinMagFilter::kNearest` (`impeller/core/sampler_descriptor.h`).
- It ignores the snapshot's own `sampler_descriptor`, which the Gaussian blur sets to linear for its downsampled output.
  - 3.47.9: [`color_matrix_filter_contents.cc#L96`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/c197ca5199e9ee5661e865596c9c07294dfab51c/engine/src/flutter/impeller/entity/contents/filters/color_matrix_filter_contents.cc#L96)
  - 3.50.0: [`#L96`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/ab2912035e160d9cad6306df307576da6128ebdb/engine/src/flutter/impeller/entity/contents/filters/color_matrix_filter_contents.cc#L96)
  - `master` on 2026-11-16: the same.
- `border_mask_blur_filter_contents.cc` and one site in `blend_filter_contents.cc` also use `GetSampler({})`. They were not checked.

Related: #196728 (the same filter also asks its input for an unbounded snapshot).

**Possible fix.** Sample with `input_snapshot->sampler_descriptor`, as other contents that draw snapshots do.

**Why it matters.** It makes every blur faded with an alpha color matrix (or tinted with a saturation matrix, like `CupertinoPopupSurface`) blocky on smooth content. Switching between the composed and the plain blur at the end of a fade then shows as a visible step.

