### Actual results

The process aborts on the first value change:

```
*** Terminating app due to uncaught exception 'NSInvalidArgumentException',
reason: '-[AXPlatformNodeCocoa startEditing]: unrecognized selector sent to instance 0x...'
```

```
CoreFoundation  -[NSObject(NSObject) doesNotRecognizeSelector:]
FlutterMacOS    flutter::AccessibilityBridgeMac::MacOSEventsFromAXEvent(ui::AXEventGenerator::Event, ui::AXNode const&) const
FlutterMacOS    flutter::AccessibilityBridgeMac::OnAccessibilityEvent(ui::AXEventGenerator::TargetedEvent)
FlutterMacOS    flutter::AccessibilityBridge::CommitUpdates()
FlutterMacOS    -[FlutterViewController updateSemantics:]
```

Cause, as far as I can tell: `SelectableText` produces a node with role `kTextField` + read-only. `FlutterPlatformNodeDelegateMac::Init` / `NodeDataChanged` give a *read-only* text field a plain `AXPlatformNode` (only editable text fields get `FlutterTextPlatformNode`). But `AccessibilityBridgeMac::MacOSEventsFromAXEvent`, case `VALUE_CHANGED`, checks only `ax_node.data().role == kTextField` and then sends `startEditing` to the native object — the `FML_DCHECK(isKindOfClass:FlutterTextField)` there would catch it in an engine debug build, but in the shipped engine it is an unrecognized selector.

Suggested fix: in `VALUE_CHANGED`, take the FlutterTextField path only when the native object is one (`[native isKindOfClass:FlutterTextField.class]`, or `IsTextField() && !IsReadOnlyOrDisabled()`), otherwise fall through to the regular `NSAccessibilityValueChangedNotification`.

Workaround: `SelectionArea(child: Text(...))` instead of `SelectableText`.

