## Expected results

`down`, `panStart`, then `up` and `panEnd` (the log lists newest first); "Pointers down: 0".

## Actual results

`down` and `panStart`, then no `up` or `panEnd`; in some trials a `hover #0 touch` line follows. "Pointers down" stays at 1 after the lift, and each later press of this kind adds 1 (2, then 3). Any recognizer holding the pointer stays active (e.g. a drag-driven auto-scroll keeps running after the finger lifts).

This happened in every trial, whether the press started on Flutter content (4 trials) or in the blue platform view (3 trials). A `hover` line appeared in 3 of the 7.

Browser events for one press on Flutter content, recorded by a capturing listener on `window` (CSS y; the view ends at 781):

```
