## Cause

In [`pointer_binding.dart`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/pointer_binding.dart) (links at master `0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b`; this path is the same in 3.47.7):

1. When the finger leaves the view while the touch is still down and uncaptured, Safari fires `pointerleave` on the view with `buttons: 0` (a WebKit bug: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=332282).
2. The view's [`pointerleave` listener](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/pointer_binding.dart#L1270-L1281) calls [`sanitizeLeaveEvent`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/pointer_binding.dart#L1037-L1049) for every pointer type. With `buttons == 0` it sets `_pressedButtons = 0` and returns `PointerChange.hover`. No `up` or `cancel` is sent.
3. Later `pointermove`s (`buttons: 1`) [become hovers](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/pointer_binding.dart#L1014-L1016). The real `pointerup` then [produces nothing](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/pointer_binding.dart#L1051-L1056) because `_pressedButtons == 0`.
4. That [`pointerup` handler](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/pointer_binding.dart#L1284-L1295) still calls [`_removePointerIfUnhoverable`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/pointer_binding.dart#L1109-L1115), which removes the device from `_downTouchDevices`. As a result, the iOS safety net [`_cancelAbandonedTouches`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/pointer_binding.dart#L1381) (#189608, for #188781) has nothing left to cancel.

On master, #195187 captures presses on Flutter content to the view and cancels them if that capture is lost, so they should no longer reach step 1. By design it [skips presses](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/0095cdb3301e0544f4f4df853af0f34f10f6b05b/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/pointer_binding.dart#L1175-L1177) on platform views, the text-editing host and the semantics host, so for those presses the path above is unchanged.

## Suggested fixes

1. Skip the leave heuristic for `pointerType == 'touch'`. A touch cannot hover; its end arrives as `pointerup` or `pointercancel`, and on iOS `_cancelAbandonedTouches` covers touches that get neither.
2. Or, when a leave clears a pressed pointer, send `up` (or `cancel`) before the hover, as `sanitizeMissingRightClickUp` does.
3. Also, remove a device from `_downTouchDevices` only once an `up` or `cancel` was actually sent, so `_cancelAbandonedTouches` can still recover it.

Possibly related: #138304 (mouse in Firefox, press stuck after leaving the window; cause not confirmed there).

