```js
const ta = document.querySelector('flt-text-editing-host textarea');
const end = ta.selectionEnd, start = end - 'wor'.length;
ta.setSelectionRange(start, end);
ta.dispatchEvent(new InputEvent('beforeinput', {inputType: 'insertReplacementText', data: 'world', bubbles: true, cancelable: true}));
ta.setRangeText('world', start, end, 'end');
ta.dispatchEvent(new InputEvent('input', {inputType: 'insertReplacementText', data: 'world', bubbles: true}));
```

Then press Backspace a few times and type a letter.

**Second variant, with text after the word:** reload, type `Hello wor and more`, and run `document.querySelector('flt-text-editing-host textarea').setSelectionRange(9, 9)` in the console. Then run the snippet above as a separate step, so that the caret move has been processed first.


### Cause

WebKit applies a suggestion in [`WebPage::applyAutocorrectionInternal`](https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/blob/a47d3db47b3f8a54014ad0bd8d5739f99bcc3137/Source/WebKit/WebProcess/WebPage/ios/WebPageIOS.mm#L2445-L2448): it sets the selection to the typed part of the word and calls `insertText` with the suggestion, synchronously. The `selectionchange` caused by the new selection is queued, so it arrives after the edit. In the engine:

1. [`handleBeforeInput`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/2fd8904afdf5438d7aee6065d550cec670ab0423/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/text_editing/text_editing.dart#L1870-L1907) takes the delta's position from `lastEditingState`. That is still the collapsed caret after `wor`, not the element's current selection, which already spans `wor`. The result is `deltaStart = deltaEnd = 9` with `deltaText = 'world'`.
2. [`inferDeltaState`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/2fd8904afdf5438d7aee6065d550cec670ab0423/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/text_editing/text_editing.dart#L841-L960) sees that the previous selection was collapsed and treats the edit as an insertion at 9. That does not reproduce the new text, so the fallback searches for `world` in the new text. The match at 6..11 extends past the old text (length 9), so [`actualEnd = match.start + deltaText.length - 1`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/2fd8904afdf5438d7aee6065d550cec670ab0423/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/text_editing/text_editing.dart#L931) is 10. The call `_replace(oldText, 'world', TextRange(start: 6, end: 10))` then evaluates `'Hello wor'.substring(10)` and throws a `RangeError`. In a debug build, the range assert in `_replace` fails instead, like in #104944.
   With text after the word, the match lies within the old text. None of the candidate ranges reproduces the new text, so the unverified insertion at 9 is sent.
3. Because `handleChange` throws, neither `lastEditingState` nor the delta state is updated: [`_editingDeltaState = null`](https://github.com/flutter/flutter/blob/2fd8904afdf5438d7aee6065d550cec670ab0423/engine/src/flutter/lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/text_editing/text_editing.dart#L1825-L1850) is never reached. Every following event is compared against the stale old text and throws the same way, until the DOM text equals that old text again.

The same code is on master (2fd8904) and in 3.50.0, which this was tested on. It was first seen on 3.47.8.

### Possible fix

- **Read the range from the element in `handleBeforeInput`.** Take the range from the element's current `selectionStart`/`selectionEnd`, not from `lastEditingState`. When that selection is not collapsed, the event replaces exactly that range. An equivalent fix: when the DOM selection differs from `lastEditingState`, process it as a selection change before handling the `beforeinput`.
- **Never send or throw on an unverified delta in `inferDeltaState`.** When no candidate reproduces the new text, fall back to a delta that is correct by construction, such as the common-prefix/common-suffix difference between the old and new text, or a replacement of the whole old text. An exception in `handleChange` leaves the engine out of step with the DOM for every following keystroke, and an unverified guess silently corrupts the client's text.

### Workaround

This script in `web/index.html` tells the engine about the selection before its own `beforeinput` listener runs. With it, the client in the code sample receives a `TextEditingDeltaNonTextUpdate` for the selection and then the correct edit, in both variants. It also fixed the Fleather case on the same replay.

```js
document.addEventListener('beforeinput', (event) => {
  const input = event.target;
  if (input.closest?.('flt-text-editing-host') &&
      input.selectionStart !== input.selectionEnd) {
    document.dispatchEvent(new Event('selectionchange'));
  }
}, {capture: true});
```

Related: #104944 (the same `_replace` range failure, reported without a cause) and #105243 (a proposed refactor of this code).


### Expected results

The client receives the change of `wor` to `world`. Its text becomes `Hello world` (or `Hello world and more` in the second variant), and the following keys keep working.

### Actual results

- **The word ends the text (`Hello wor`):** `handleChange` throws a `RangeError` (stack below), and the client receives nothing. Its text stays `Hello wor` while the textarea holds `Hello world`. Every following `input` event throws too, backspaces and letters alike, until the textarea's text is back to `Hello wor`. Only then does editing work again. On the iPhone this looks like: the suggestion does nothing, and neither do the next few backspaces and letters.
- **Text follows the word (`Hello wor and more`):** nothing is thrown, but the client receives a `TextEditingDeltaInsertion` of `world` at offset 9. Its text becomes `Hello worworld and more` while the textarea holds `Hello world and more`.

`TextField` is not affected, because it does not use the delta model. We hit this with the [Fleather](https://pub.dev/packages/fleather) rich-text editor (`enableDeltaModel: true`), where the symptoms on a real iPhone 16 match the first variant exactly.

