### Steps to reproduce

When a Material `RangeSlider` is placed inside a scrollable viewport (such as a `SingleChildScrollView` or `CustomScrollView` inside a mid-height bottom sheet) and is initially clipped offscreen below the viewport fold, navigating onto its thumbs via iOS VoiceOver swipe navigation announces the thumb values (e.g. `"20%, adjustable"`, `"80%, adjustable"`) without scrolling the `RangeSlider` into view. VoiceOver's focus cursor remains stuck near the bottom edge of the viewport until focus advances past the `RangeSlider` onto a standard widget-backed element (such as a `Text` label).

### Root Cause Analysis
1. In `packages/material_ui/lib/src/range_slider.dart` (`_RenderRangeSlider.assembleSemanticsNode`), the two thumb nodes are instantiated manually as bare `SemanticsNode()` objects without a `showOnScreen` callback:
   ```dart
   _startSemanticsNode ??= SemanticsNode();
   _endSemanticsNode ??= SemanticsNode();
   ```
   (Compare `RenderTable.assembleSemanticsNode` in `packages/flutter/lib/src/rendering/table.dart`, which passes `showOnScreen: () { showOnScreen(descendant: this, rect: rowBox); }`.)
2. Because `_startSemanticsNode` and `_endSemanticsNode` are not backed by child `RenderObject`s in `_RenderObjectSemantics` (`PipelineOwner.flushSemantics`), Flutter never computes `SemanticsFlag.isHidden` against ancestor `semanticsClipRect` / `paintClipRect` for those child nodes, and `_createSemanticsConfiguration` never sets `config.isHidden` or `config.onShowOnScreen`.
3. On iOS (`SemanticsObject.mm`, `accessibilityElementDidBecomeFocused`), the accessibility bridge only calls `[self showOnScreen]` when `self.node.flags.isHidden || self.node.flags.isHeader`, and dispatches `SemanticsAction::kShowOnScreen` to the thumb node's `uid` — which no-ops in `SemanticsOwner.performAction` because both `_showOnScreen` and `onShowOnScreen` are `null`.

### Expected results

Focusing either offscreen `RangeSlider` thumb scrolls the enclosing scrollable so the thumb becomes visible on screen, and `tester.semantics.showOnScreen(...)` scrolls the viewport.

### Actual results

Neither thumb scrolls into view when focused by VoiceOver (`showOnScreen` is a no-op), and offscreen thumb `SemanticsNode`s report `SemanticsFlag.isHidden == false`.

