Flutter 3.47.7 (framework abaf9c5237), Windows and macOS desktop.

## What happens

`OverlayPortal` links the overlay child's semantics node to the anchor through
`traversalParentIdentifier` / `traversalChildIdentifier`: the overlay node is listed in
traversal order under whatever node the anchor's annotation ends up in. If that link
is lost, the overlay node stays in the tree (it is still a child of the overlay's own
parent) but no node lists it in traversal order. The engine's accessibility bridge then
rejects the whole update:

    Failed to update ui::AXTree ... Nodes left pending: 41

From then on, the platform's accessibility tree stops following the app, on Windows
(MSAA) and macOS (AX). In our app, a screen reader saw an empty task list after one
row's menu had been opened.

The link is lost in three cases:

1. The anchor is under `Opacity(opacity: 0)` (or a `FadeTransition` at 0) without
   `alwaysIncludeSemantics`. This is common during a fade-out or a cross-fade.
2. The anchor is under `ExcludeSemantics`, or under the `BlockSemantics` of a dialog.
3. The portal sits inside another portal's anchor, without a semantics boundary between
   them. Both anchors annotate the same node, which keeps only one traversal parent
   identifier.

Desktop apps only show the error while an assistive client has turned semantics on
(a screen reader or an accessibility inspector). That is why it went unnoticed in
ordinary runs.

## Minimal reproduction

`overlay_portal_semantics_repro_test.dart` (below). It has no dependencies beyond
flutter_test. A node counts as orphaned when it is reachable through `visitChildren` but
not through `debugListChildrenInOrder(DebugSemanticsDumpOrder.traversalOrder)`.

| case | orphaned nodes |
|---|---|
| anchor under `Opacity(0)` | 2 |
| anchor under `ExcludeSemantics` | 2 |
| portal inside another portal's anchor | 2 |
| control: plain portal | 0 |

## Expected

An overlay whose anchor is excluded is either excluded with it, or listed under the
nearest node that is kept. Two portals whose anchors fall in one node both keep their
overlays listed. Either way, the update stays valid.

## Workarounds we use

- Give each anchor a node of its own (`Semantics(container: true)` around the portal).
- Keep the portal in the tree only while its overlay shows. A controller shown in
  `initState` is shown from the first frame.
- Use `alwaysIncludeSemantics: true` on opacity transitions an anchor can pass through.

## Reproduction test

```dart
import 'package:flutter/rendering.dart';
import 'package:flutter/widgets.dart';
import 'package:flutter_test/flutter_test.dart';

class Portal extends StatefulWidget {
  const Portal({super.key, required this.label, this.child});
  final String label;
  final Widget? child;
  @override
  State<Portal> createState() => _PortalState();
}

class _PortalState extends State<Portal> {
  final controller = OverlayPortalController()..show();
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => OverlayPortal(
        controller: controller,
        overlayChildBuilder: (_) => Align(child: Text(widget.label)),
        child: widget.child ?? const SizedBox(width: 10, height: 10),
      );
}

Widget app(Widget body) => Directionality(
      textDirection: TextDirection.ltr,
      child: Overlay(initialEntries: [OverlayEntry(builder: (_) => Center(child: body))]),
    );

/// Nodes in the semantics tree that no parent lists in traversal order:
/// the engine rejects a whole update holding one.
List<SemanticsNode> orphans() {
  final kept = <SemanticsNode>{};
  final listed = <SemanticsNode>{};
  void keep(SemanticsNode n) {
    kept.add(n);
    n.visitChildren((c) {
      keep(c);
      return true;
    });
  }

  void list(SemanticsNode n) {
    listed.add(n);
    n.debugListChildrenInOrder(DebugSemanticsDumpOrder.traversalOrder).forEach(list);
  }

  void visit(PipelineOwner owner) {
    if (owner.semanticsOwner?.rootSemanticsNode case final root?) {
      keep(root);
      list(root);
    }
    owner.visitChildren(visit);
  }

  visit(RendererBinding.instance.rootPipelineOwner);
  return [...kept.difference(listed)];
}

void main() {
  testWidgets('anchor under Opacity(0)', (tester) async {
    await tester.pumpWidget(app(const Opacity(opacity: 0, child: Portal(label: 'overlay'))));
    debugPrint('opacity0 orphans: ${orphans().length}');
  });
  testWidgets('anchor under ExcludeSemantics', (tester) async {
    await tester.pumpWidget(app(const ExcludeSemantics(child: Portal(label: 'overlay'))));
    debugPrint('exclude orphans: ${orphans().length}');
  });
  testWidgets('portal inside another portal\'s anchor', (tester) async {
    await tester.pumpWidget(app(const Portal(label: 'outer', child: Portal(label: 'inner'))));
    debugPrint('nested orphans: ${orphans().length}');
  });
  testWidgets('control: plain portal', (tester) async {
    await tester.pumpWidget(app(const Portal(label: 'overlay')));
    debugPrint('plain orphans: ${orphans().length}');
  });
}
```

