Nothing is pasted. The key down reaches `HardwareKeyboard` while the root scope still has focus; focus goes back to the text field only a few milliseconds later, in time for the key up:

```text
8747 ms  lifecycle resumed
8754 ms  KeyDownEvent V, focus: root scope
8756 ms  focus -> TextField
8757 ms  KeyUpEvent V, focus: TextField
```

When the app becomes inactive, `FocusManager._appLifecycleChange` parks focus on the root scope and applies that change right away. On `resumed` it only calls `_suspendedNode!.requestFocus()`, which schedules `applyFocusChangesIfNeeded` as a microtask. On macOS the UI and platform threads are merged, so `Shell::OnPlatformViewDispatchPlatformMessage` runs the lifecycle message synchronously through `fml::TaskRunner::RunNowAndFlushMessages`, and the microtasks only run when the empty task it posts gets its turn. The key event comes in over `flutter/keydata` the same way, and can be dispatched before that task runs.

I have a fix that applies the restore synchronously, like the suspend path already does, and will open a PR. The other half of the launcher problem, the side-less command flag, is #178609 / #196769.

