### Expected results

No validation error: the samplers the compiler removed are left out of the reflection, or at least never share a binding.

### Actual results

The draw itself comes out right (`[255, 255, 0, 255]`), but the validation layer reports:

```
Severity: Error
ID Name: VUID-VkDescriptorSetLayoutCreateInfo-binding-00279
Trigger: vkCreateDescriptorSetLayout(): pCreateInfo->pBindings[3].binding is duplicated at pBindings[0].binding.
```

The shader bundle's reflection shows why. On every backend (metal_ios, metal_desktop, opengl_es, opengl_desktop, vulkan) the fragment shader's textures are:

```
used_a    set 0  binding 64
used_d    set 0  binding 65
unused_b  set 0  binding 0
unused_c  set 0  binding 0
```

The compiled code drops `unused_b` and `unused_c`, but the reflection keeps them, both at binding 0. `ShaderLibrary` (lib/gpu/shader_library.cc) adds a `DescriptorSetLayout` entry for each reflected texture, and `PipelineVK` (impeller/renderer/backend/vulkan/pipeline_vk.cc) turns each into a `VkDescriptorSetLayoutBinding` without removing duplicates.

Shaders that include a shared file declaring samplers they don't all read meet this easily. Workaround: declare only the samplers a stage actually reads.

