### Expected results

Red `[255, 0, 0, 255]` in every read: work submitted earlier is visible to the readback.

### Actual results

Galaxy S10 (SM-G973F, Exynos 9820, Mali-G76, Android 12, Vulkan 1.1), 3 runs of 40 trials:

| read | red (right) | `[0, 0, 0, 0]` |
| --- | --- | --- |
| right after submit | 55 | 5 (1, 2 and 2 per run) |
| after the completion callback | 60 | 0 |

The zeros are not even the clear value. The validation layer reports nothing. With a single submission (pass 1 only, reading A right away), all 40 reads were right in each of 2 runs, so it seems to need a texture rendered in one submission and sampled in the next.

`CommandBuffer::Submit` (lib/gpu/command_buffer.cc) hands each buffer straight to the Vulkan queue. My guess, not proven, is that nothing orders the first submission's color writes before the second's sampling, or the second's writes before the readback's copy, on this driver. I have not tried another Vulkan device.

Workaround: wait for the completion callback before reading back.

Possibly related: #195250 (device lost on Adreno when a depth pass is sampled by the next pass in the same command buffer).

