### Summary

When a background color (or any other paint-only style) moves to a different range of a paragraph, SkParagraph shapes the whole paragraph again, although the text and the fonts did not change. The paragraph cache misses because its key compares the positions of the style blocks, and a highlight on a different word is different blocks.

This is the main cost of a "find in page" highlight that is applied through `TextSpan`s: every text whose matches change is shaped again on every change of the query.

### Reproduction

`dart:ui` only. Run in profile mode, for example `flutter run --profile -d macos`.

