With Impeller the stacked arcs come out blotchy and broken, with hard light and dark pixels and a strange dark wedge in the middle of the stack. With Skia they are clean, evenly spaced bands.

I see it at stroke widths 0.5, 1.0 and 1.5. At 2.5 both engines fill the stack in solid, so there is not much to compare there. It is the same whether I use `drawArc` or `drawPath`, with or without a fill underneath, and at a whole pixel or half pixel offset. A single small oval on its own looks fine in both engines. It seems to need several thin arcs close together (10 arcs, 1.9 px apart).

This is at device pixel ratio 1.0. On a screen with more pixels I don't notice it.

I found #187537 and #191171, which sound like the same thing, and the fix in #191379 is in 3.50. I still see it on 3.50.1 though. I'm not sure if this is something that fix missed or a different problem. For now I turned Impeller off in my Linux runner with `fl_dart_project_set_enable_impeller(project, FALSE)`.

