The sample opens one `RegularWindow` beside the main window 2 s after start, lets it draw for 1 s, takes it out of the widget tree (`ViewAnchor.view` set to null), waits for two frames (`SchedulerBinding.endOfFrame` twice) and only then calls `RegularWindowController.destroy()`, then exits 0 a second later.

