# [web/skwasm] Mutating a Path after drawing it corrupts native memory (use-after-free)

## Summary
On the skwasm renderer (dart2wasm, Flutter 3.47.9, engine 89c39edf), a `Path` that has already been drawn can be mutated and drawn again. The mutation disposes the native path object that is still in use. The next draw, or the frame-end `frameArena.collect()`, then uses or frees freed memory. Symptoms are `RuntimeError: memory access out of bounds`, `unreachable`, `null function`, or `operation does not support unaligned accesses` in `skwasm.wasm`, and a hung tab. CanvasKit is not affected.

## Root cause (engine, from reading the source)
- `lib/web_ui/lib/src/engine/primitives/path.dart`: `EnginePath._addCommand` calls `_invalidateCachedPath()`, which calls `_cachedPath?.dispose()`.
- `skwasm/skwasm_impl/path.dart`: `SkwasmPath.build()` returns `this`, so the cached builder and the built path are the same native object.
- So disposing the built path also frees the builder that `_cachedBuilder` still references. Subsequent `addPath` or `drawPath` use freed memory.

## Minimal repro (complete, runnable)

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

class P extends CustomPainter {
  final Path path = Path();
  final double t;
  P(this.t);
  @override
  void paint(Canvas canvas, Size size) {
    path.reset();
    path.addRect(Rect.fromLTWH(0, 0, 50 + t * 10, 50));
    canvas.drawPath(path, Paint()..color = Colors.blue);
    path.addRect(Rect.fromLTWH(60, 60, 50 + t * 10, 50));
    canvas.drawPath(path, Paint()..color = Colors.red);
  }
  @override
  bool shouldRepaint(covariant P old) => true;
}

void main() => runApp(const MaterialApp(home: Scaffold(body: _Anim())));

class _Anim extends StatefulWidget {
  const _Anim();
  @override
  State<_Anim> createState() => _AnimState();
}

class _AnimState extends State<_Anim> with SingleTickerProviderStateMixin {
  late final AnimationController c = AnimationController(vsync: this, duration: const Duration(milliseconds: 400))..repeat();
  @override
  void dispose() { c.dispose(); super.dispose(); }
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) => Center(
        child: AnimatedBuilder(
          animation: c,
          builder: (_, __) => CustomPaint(painter: P(c.value), size: const Size(200, 200)),
        ),
      );
}
```

Build and serve: `flutter build web --wasm --release`, then open the page in Chrome. Within about 20 seconds the console shows `Uncaught RuntimeError: memory access out of bounds` in `skwasm.wasm` and the page stops drawing.

## Real-world trigger
`s_packages` 8.0.0 `Glow2` (`_Glow2Painter`) kept a cached `Path`, reset it, and called `addPath` once per glow ring before each `drawPath`. With `glowCount: 2` it crashed on skwasm. Changing the draw to `canvas.drawPath(Path.from(_glowPath), paint)` fixed it.

## Related
Similar skwasm trap, closed without a repro: #184858 (paragraphBuilder_dispose during rebuilds). This report includes a complete repro.

## Environment
- Flutter 3.47.9 (stable), Dart 3.13.7, dart2wasm + skwasm, Chromium (Chrome 158, macOS).
- Single-threaded skwasm (page not cross-origin isolated).

## Suggested fix
Do not dispose the built path when the builder is still referenced, or make `SkwasmPath.build()` return a separate object so the two can be disposed independently. Add a skwasm test that mutates a path after drawing it.
